{
  "$comment": [
    "Reference vectors for the clinical calculation library (CP43).",
    "Consumed by BOTH the Go suite (backend/internal/clinical/calc) and the TypeScript suite",
    "(packages/clinical-calc). A disagreement between them fails CI, which is the point:",
    "two implementations of CKD-EPI that disagree is a patient-safety bug.",
    "",
    "Every expected value was computed independently from the published equation, not read",
    "off either implementation. A fixture derived from the code would prove only that the",
    "code agrees with itself.",
    "",
    "tolerance is absolute, on the value as given. It is 1e-9 rather than exact because the",
    "two runtimes order floating-point operations differently and pow() is not required to",
    "be correctly rounded in either."
  ],
  "tolerance": 1e-9,
  "cases": {
    "bmi": [
      {
        "name": "a 80 kg adult of 180 cm",
        "inputs": {
          "weight_kg": 80,
          "height_cm": 180
        },
        "expected": 24.691358024691358
      },
      {
        "name": "a 45 kg adult of 150 cm",
